## Finding taxonomy (the scan output)

Every finding is one row. Tags are closed. Replacement is mandatory except `delete`.

| Tag | Detector (deterministic) | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `reuse` | Symbol / function with equivalent signature already in-graph, inbound >= 1, this copy has inbound 0 or 1 | Second `formatMoney` in `ui/utils.ts` |
| `stdlib` | Hand-rolled helper whose body matches a stdlib / language-pack fingerprint | 20-line deep clone vs `structuredClone` / `copy.deepcopy` |
| `native` | Dep or component whose only call sites are a platform primitive | `flatpickr` wrapping one date field; `moment` for one `format` |
| `yagni` | Interface / abstract type with exactly one implementation; factory with one product; config key read in one place with a literal default never overridden | `AbstractRepository` + `JpaRepositoryImpl` only |
| `wrapper` | File / class whose public methods only delegate (fan-out 1, no extra logic) | `DatePickerService` → `FlatpickrAdapter` → lib |
| `dead_flex` | Feature flag, extra param, unused generic type parameter with zero runtime readers | `enableExperimentalCache` never read |
| `newdep` | Direct dependency whose call-site count is <= 2 and a stdlib/native equivalent exists | `qs` next to `URLSearchParams` |
| `shrink` | Same control flow, shorter form available from a mechanical rewrite table | manual loop → `dict(zip)` / stream collect |

Out of scope (do not emit, route to the owning playbook):

| Signal | Owner |
|---|---|
| Taint / injection / authn / crypto / secrets | `repo_health_audit` Stage 4 |
| CVE / license / EOL | `repo_health_audit` Stage 2 + dependency-intelligence suite |
| Flaky tests, coverage gaps | `repo_health_audit` Stage 3 |
| Breaking API contract | `repo_health_audit` Stage 8 |
| "This might be cleaner if we..." with no graph evidence | discarded |

Confidence:
- `confirmed` — EXTRACTED graph evidence (counts, lockfile, AST match). Emit.
- `heuristic` — INFERRED / AMBIGUOUS / regex-only. **Do not emit** as a finding. May appear in `signals_suppressed`.

That is the determinism bar. Same rule as `repo_health_audit`.

