## Orchestrator + batch wiring

Single repo:

```bash
python codemind_batch.py run \
  --base-url "$ORCH_BASE_URL" \
  --input repos.csv \
  --playbooks lean_codescan \
  --goal "scan for over-engineering" \
  --state ./cm_state_lean
```

Composed estate sweep (one index, two docs):

```bash
python codemind_batch.py run \
  --base-url "$ORCH_BASE_URL" \
  --input repos.csv \
  --playbooks repo_health_audit,lean_codescan \
  --goal "health + lean scan" \
  --state ./cm_state_nightly
```

CI / PR:

```
on: pull_request
job: orchestrator.run
  playbook_names: [lean_codescan]
  options.mode: incremental_pr
  gate: fail if any finding.tag == newdep AND ccc_tier <= 2 AND cut_deps >= 1
  comment: "<path>:L<line>: <tag> <what>. <replacement>."
```

Quality gate is optional and narrow. Default CI is comment-only. Do not block merges on `shrink` or `yagni` until false-positive rate is measured for two sprints.

Webhook after persist:

```
lean_codescan.completed
  repo_id, commit_sha, run_id, summary.net_loc, summary.net_deps
```

Downstream: Discovery UI, TABR board, optional patch job.

